On a second look, I realised that the documentation for the 2.0.x is 
even worse than what I remembered and I dashed too quickly to a Read The 
Fine Manual type of answer.

By default, there no specific environment for base (and no feature for 
having a namespace per module on the Python side).

Try:
robjects.r("base::matrix")

